-- Transcription of layout-language-consult.md §5.2 (lines 521-529),
-- H(V(B,A),I). Disclosed adjustments (full list in the build report):
--   - the document elides sizing on the ROOT slot entirely (it just
--     writes `layout q5go = H(...)` with no leading `{...}`) for all five
--     §5 encodings. Every Slot in lyt_ast requires a Sizing, and the
--     compiler pins the root's width/height to the screen class's
--     dimensions regardless of its declared Sizing (§6 "Root:
--     w_root = W_c, h_root = H_c", line 626) — so the root's sizing values
--     are inert. We supply a no-op placeholder, {min 0, pref 1fr, max inf}.
--   - sizing moved to precede its node (`{pref 1fr} V(...)` instead of the
--     document's `V(...) {pref 1fr}`), matching the EBNF's own stated
--     production order `slot ::= presence? sizing node` (line 277).
--   - `pref maximize` resolved by the loader to `pref 1fr`; the actual
--     maximize-area objective term is wired in Python by the runner
--     (objectivesec has no worked concrete syntax anywhere in §5).
--   - `I[info]` puts a facet name where the grammar expects a domain
--     (see loader.py `_load_leaf`); resolved to domain='common',
--     facets={'info'}.
--   - min/max omitted on B's sizing default to 0px / inf (disclosed
--     general completion rule).
layout q5go =
  {min 0px, pref 1fr, max inf} H(
    {pref 1fr} V(
      {pref maximize, aspect 1} B[board],
      {min 28px, pref 28px, max 28px} A[board, action]
    ),
    {min 40ch, pref 48ch, max 60ch} I[info]
  )
